---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const links = {
  catchup: `${base}/performance-improvements/bounded-catchup`,
  scaling: `${base}/horizontal-scale`,
  loadTests: `${base}/load-testing`,
  issue5: "https://gecgithub01.walmart.com/GPA/chronicle/issues/5",
  adr5: "https://github.com/adityavkk/chronicle/blob/main/docs/adr/0004-bounded-read-pages-and-snapshot-catch-up.md",
  evidence: "https://github.com/adityavkk/chronicle/blob/main/docs/benchmarks/issue-5-bounded-catchup.md",
  comparison: "https://github.com/adityavkk/chronicle/blob/main/docs/benchmarks/ds-bench/configuration-comparison.md",
};
---

<div class="improvements">
  <article class="improvement featured">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      <span class="status">validated</span>
    </div>
    <h3>Bounded catch-up</h3>
    <p class="result">128 errors to 435 complete measured replays</p>
    <p>
      Redis fetches one frame, then optionally bulk-fetches only the range that
      fits the remaining 1 MiB target. A separate 1,024-frame cap bounds each
      page, and Chronicle writes each frame directly to the client.
    </p>
    <nav aria-label="Bounded catch-up links">
      <a class="primary" href={links.catchup}>Read the explainer <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={links.issue5}>GPA/chronicle issue #5 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href={links.adr5}>Architecture decision <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href={links.evidence}>Evidence report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </nav>
  </article>

  <article class="improvement">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      <span class="status">shipped</span>
    </div>
    <h3>Horizontal scale</h3>
    <p class="result">12.48 to 12.61 ms fanout p99 from 1 to 8 replicas</p>
    <p>
      Chronicle homes subscription state by Redis slot and divides claim work.
      The cloud curve stayed flat through eight replicas. Quota blocked the
      12 replica point and the cloud run with multiple shards.
    </p>
    <nav aria-label="Horizontal scale links">
      <a class="primary" href={links.scaling}>Read the scaling report <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={links.loadTests}>Open the cloud load tests <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </nav>
  </article>

  <article class="improvement">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      <span class="status">measured</span>
    </div>
    <h3>Configurations and systems</h3>
    <p class="result">Chronicle compared with Ursula, Rust, and Node</p>
    <p>
      The benchmark record separates Chronicle node size, Redis size, replica
      count, durability, and workload shape. Historical replay remains
      Chronicle's largest measured gap.
    </p>
    <nav aria-label="Configuration comparison links">
      <a class="primary" href={links.comparison}>Open the comparison report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a href={links.loadTests}>Read the load test method <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</div>

<style lang="scss">
  .improvements {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .improvement {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 22px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }
  .improvement.featured::before {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    width: 3px;
    content: "";
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .num { color: var(--accent); }
  .status {
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(36, 131, 123, 0.35);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    background: var(--accent-tint);
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .result {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  p {
    margin: 16px 0 22px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  nav {
    display: grid;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
  }
  a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  a.primary {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .improvements { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
